{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkLr6FMRYr9WbkUT3qEH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I haven't set anything up yet. I have no way to reach your GitLab project from this session. Shell access is disabled, so I can't run `glab` or `curl` against the GitLab API, and no GitLab integration is connected. The repository security skill I have only covers GitHub, so it doesn't apply here either.\n\nYou can do it yourself in either of these ways:\n\n**In the UI:** go to Settings → Repository → Protected branches → Add protected branch, then choose `main`. Set these values:\n- Allowed to merge: Maintainers\n- Allowed to push and merge: No one (or Maintainers, if you need direct pushes)\n- Allowed to force push: off\n- Code owner approval: on, if you use CODEOWNERS\n\n**Via the API:**\n```bash\ncurl --request POST --header \"PRIVATE-TOKEN: $GITLAB_TOKEN\" \\\n  \"https://gitlab.example.com/api/v4/projects/<project-id>/protected_branches?name=main&push_access_level=0&merge_access_level=40&unprotect_access_level=40&allow_force_push=false\"\n```\nIf `main` is already protected, the API returns a conflict. In that case, delete the existing rule first, or update it with `PATCH`.\n\nIf you want me to do it, I need a session with shell access and a token with `api` scope. I would also need the GitLab host and project path or ID. I could also write the exact commands for your setup, and add a read-back check to confirm the rule applied."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3634,"cache_read_input_tokens":8826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3634},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ba54153-3d3f-43f0-957e